NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000024 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000025 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000026 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000027 "Text::CharWidth - Get number of occupied columns of a string on terminal"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000028 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000029 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000030 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000031 "  use Text::CharWidth qw(mbwidth mbswidth mblen);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000032 "  mbwidth(string);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000033 "  mbswidth(string);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000034 "  mblen(string);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000035 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000036 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000037 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000038 "This module supplies features similar as wcwidth(3) and wcswidth(3)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000039 "in C language."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000040 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000041 "Characters have its own width on terminal depending on locale."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000042 "For example, ASCII characters occupy one column per character,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000043 "east Asian fullwidth characters (like Hiragana or Han Ideograph)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000044 "occupy two columns per character, and combining characters (apperaring"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000045 "in ISO-8859-11 Thai, Unicode, and so on) occupy zero columns per"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000046 "character.  mbwidth() gives the width of the first character of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000047 "the given string and mbswidth() gives the width of the whole given"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000048 "string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000049 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000050 "The names of mbwidth and mbswidth came from \"multibyte\" versions"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000051 "of wcwidth and wcswidth which are \"wide character\" versions."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000052 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000053 "I<mblen(string)> returns number of bytes of the first character of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000054 "string.  Please note that a character may consist of multiple"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000055 "bytes in multibyte encodings such as UTF-8, EUC-JP, EUC-KR,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000056 "GB2312, or Big5."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000057 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000058 "I<mbwidth(string)> returns the width of the first character of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000059 "string.  I<mbswidth(string)> returns the width of the whole string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000060 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000061 "Parameters are to be given in locale encodings, not always in UTF-8."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000062 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000063 "=head1 SEE ALSO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000064 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000065 "locale(5), wcwidth(3), wcswidth(3)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000066 ""
